The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (p->userfont)
    old_data = vc->vc_font.data;
```
```c
if (ret)
    goto err_out;
```
```c
p->fontdata = data;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code only restores the font data if the font being set is a user font (`if (p->userfont)`). If `vc_resize()` fails, the `goto err_out` statement is executed, but the internal font data (`old_data`) is not restored, leading to potential access of invalid memory on subsequent font operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
u8 *old_data = vc->vc_font.data;
```
```c
p->fontdata = old_data;
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that `old_data` is always initialized to the current font data (`vc->vc_font.data`), regardless of whether it is a user font or not. This guarantees that the internal font data is restored correctly in the error handling section, preventing access to invalid memory and potential system crashes.

